# 🪟 Windows Security Fundamentals

## Windows Security Features
Built‑in tools protecting device, data, identity, and network.

## Windows Update / Patch Tuesday
Monthly security patches fixing vulnerabilities.

## Microsoft Defender
Built‑in antivirus with real‑time protection and scheduled scans.

## Definition vs Driver Updates
Definition updates improve malware detection.  
Driver updates improve hardware compatibility.

## Windows Security App
Central hub for antivirus, firewall, device security, and account protection.

## Full Scan Duration
Full scan may take ~1 hour because it checks all files and processes.

## Automatic Scanning
Defender automatically performs real‑time and scheduled scans.

---

## Controlled Folder Access
Blocks unauthorized apps from modifying protected folders.  
Helps prevent ransomware.

## Exclusions
Files or folders skipped during scans to reduce false positives.

---

## Windows Firewall
Controls incoming/outgoing traffic like a security guard.

### Firewall Profiles
Domain — corporate networks  
Private — home networks  
Public — public Wi‑Fi (strictest)

### Open Firewall Console
WF.msc

---

## App & Browser Control
SmartScreen blocks unsafe websites, downloads, and apps.

## Exploit Protection
Prevents common exploit techniques.

## Memory Integrity (Core Isolation)
Blocks malicious code from injecting into high‑security processes.

---

## Trusted Platform Module (TPM)
Hardware security chip storing cryptographic keys.  
Tamper‑resistant.

## BitLocker
Full‑disk encryption protecting data if device is lost or stolen.

### TPM + BitLocker
Strongest protection: secure key storage + tamper detection.

### Systems Without TPM
Startup key stored on USB drive.

---

## Volume Shadow Copy Service (VSS)
Creates point‑in‑time snapshots for backup.  
Stored in System Volume Information.

### Why Malware Deletes VSS
To prevent recovery and force ransom payment.

---

## Living Off The Land (LOTL)
Attackers use built‑in Windows tools (PowerShell, WMI) to avoid detection.

---

## Antimalware Scan Interface (AMSI)
Scans scripts before execution to detect malicious behavior.

## Credential Guard
Protects login secrets using virtualization‑based security.

## Windows Hello
Biometric authentication: face, fingerprint, PIN.

## Top Windows 10 Security Features
Credential Guard  
Device Guard  
Windows Hello  
Exploit Protection  
Secure Boot

---

# 🗂️ Active Directory Fundamentals

Active Directory is a centralized directory storing users, computers, groups, and resources.

## Windows Domain
Group of users and computers managed centrally.

## Domain Controller (DC)
Server running Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS).

## Core of Windows Domain
AD DS handles authentication, authorization, and directory objects.

## AD Objects
Users — people/services  
Groups — permission sets  
Machines — computer accounts  
Printers — shared printing resources  
Shares — shared folders/files

## Machine Accounts
End with $ to identify computer objects.

## Organizational Units (OUs)
Containers organizing users and computers.

## OUs vs Security Groups
OUs apply policies.  
Security Groups grant permissions.

## Domain Admins
Full control over all domain resources.

## Delegation
Granting specific administrative permissions to users.

