# 🌐 Networking Basics

Browser acts as client requesting webpage.  
Server responds with requested content.

## Protocol
Language computers use to communicate.

## Request & Response
Two parts of client‑server communication.

## Port
Identifies specific service (e.g., 80 = HTTP, 443 = HTTPS).

## DNS
DNS is like GPS.  
IP is the home address.  
DNS resolves domain names into IP addresses.

## HTTPS
Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure.

## Cookies vs Tokens
Cookies store session data in browser.  
Tokens identify session securely and statelessly.

## HTTP
Protocol for web communication.  
GET method requests data → 200 OK.

## URL Components
Scheme  
Host  
Filename  
Address  
Status

